    {
      "section": {
        "section_id": "sec_0395",
        "title": "Sinogram Affirmed Iterative Reconstruction (SAFIRE) / Advanced Modeled Iterative Reconstruction (ADMIRE)",
        "hierarchy_level": 3,
        "hierarchy_path": "/Dose management and optimization/Dose optimization features/Sinogram Affirmed Iterative Reconstruction (SAFIRE) / Advanced Modeled Iterative Reconstruction (ADMIRE)",
        "page_start": 195,
        "page_end": 196,
        "parent_section_id": "sec_0384",
        "child_sections": [],
        "node_count": 20,
        "confidence": 1.0,
        "structural_source": "toc",
        "flagged_for_review": false,
        "verification_score": 94.23076923076923,
        "verification_reason": "",
        "numbering_scheme": "arabic",
        "offset_applied": 0,
        "semantic_order_start": 4169,
        "semantic_order_end": 4188,
        "semantic_nodes": [
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4161",
            "canonical_text": "HandCARE is a function for reducing the dose to the hand of the operator and patient during a CT intervention by switching off the radiation for a fixed sector during the tube rotation. It is available only in the i-Sequence and i-Fluoro modes.",
            "semantic_order": 4169,
            "node_type": "paragraph",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 198.85389709472656,
              "y0": 717.1072998046875,
              "x1": 538.1702270507812,
              "y1": 684.3233032226562
            }
          },
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4162",
            "canonical_text": "You can select three different positions to switch off the exposure: 10:00, 12:00, and 2:00 o' clock. These positions usually correspond to the user-preferred side or entry point during the procedure.",
            "semantic_order": 4170,
            "node_type": "paragraph",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 198.41305541992188,
              "y0": 675.1072998046875,
              "x1": 538.4600830078125,
              "y1": 642.3233032226562
            }
          },
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4163",
            "canonical_text": "10:00 o'clock",
            "semantic_order": 4171,
            "node_type": "paragraph",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 199.0963134765625,
              "y0": 427.8353271484375,
              "x1": 267.92669677734375,
              "y1": 419.48333740234375
            }
          },
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4164",
            "canonical_text": "12:00 o'clock",
            "semantic_order": 4172,
            "node_type": "paragraph",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 199.09632873535156,
              "y0": 415.8353271484375,
              "x1": 267.92669677734375,
              "y1": 407.48333740234375
            }
          },
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4165",
            "canonical_text": "2:00 o'clock",
            "semantic_order": 4173,
            "node_type": "paragraph",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 199.09632873535156,
              "y0": 403.8353271484375,
              "x1": 262.7427062988281,
              "y1": 395.48333740234375
            }
          },
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4166",
            "canonical_text": "For information on using HandCARE, see ( Page 405 Setting a tube position for HandCARE) .",
            "semantic_order": 4174,
            "node_type": "paragraph",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 198.92494201660156,
              "y0": 385.8353271484375,
              "x1": 513.7360229492188,
              "y1": 365.39544677734375
            }
          },
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4167",
            "canonical_text": "The use of HandCARE results in a slower frame rate for image display when using the i-Fluoro mode. It still permits continuous visualization and tracking of the needle.",
            "semantic_order": 4175,
            "node_type": "paragraph",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 198.54696655273438,
              "y0": 346.2994384765625,
              "x1": 529.1830444335938,
              "y1": 325.51544189453125
            }
          },
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4168",
            "canonical_text": "5.1.7 Sinogram Affirmed Iterative Reconstruction (SAFIRE) /\r\n() g\r\nAdvanced Modeled Iterative Reconstruction (ADMIRE)",
            "semantic_order": 4176,
            "node_type": "heading",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 157.26165771484375,
              "y0": 290.8021240234375,
              "x1": 498.15057373046875,
              "y1": 267.6181335449219
            }
          },
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4169",
            "canonical_text": "Iterative reconstruction approaches allow decoupling of spatial resolution and image noise.",
            "semantic_order": 4177,
            "node_type": "paragraph",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 199.05979919433594,
              "y0": 253.0494384765625,
              "x1": 504.1327209472656,
              "y1": 232.2654266357422
            }
          },
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4170",
            "canonical_text": "With the Sinogram Affirmed Iterative Reconstruction (SAFIRE) or the Advanced Modeled Iterative Reconstruction (ADMIRE), correction loops are introduced into the image generation process. These iteration loops utilize raw-data information to significantly improve image quality.",
            "semantic_order": 4178,
            "node_type": "paragraph",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 198.72679138183594,
              "y0": 223.2474365234375,
              "x1": 537.8308715820312,
              "y1": 178.2654266357422
            }
          },
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4171",
            "canonical_text": "Additionally, image noise is removed in the iterative corrections without degrading image sharpness. The noise texture of the images is comparable to the standard convolution kernels.",
            "semantic_order": 4179,
            "node_type": "paragraph",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 198.54721069335938,
              "y0": 169.0494384765625,
              "x1": 523.1591796875,
              "y1": 138.200439453125
            }
          },
          {
            "node_id": "#/texts/4172",
            "canonical_text": "SAFIRE or ADMIRE results in an improved image quality with reduced noise and increased image sharpness.",
            "semantic_order": 4180,
            "node_type": "paragraph",
            "page_no": 195,
            "bbox": {
              "x0": 198.90721130371094,
              "y0": 127.04943084716797,
              "x1": 537.7921142578125,
              "y1": 106.26543426513672
            }
          },
